-- title:
--   Uₚ acts as p Frob⁻¹ on the Igusa component
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$.
--
--   *Cyclotomic and function-field frame.* Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(q)\!)$ with $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of `LaurentSeries L` generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-function field of $X_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), assumed non-zero; [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) is the resulting two-chart model over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, assumed proper.
--
--   *Special fibre and its two components.* Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra, and let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ over $k$ into the base change of the two-chart model to $k$. The hypotheses `hcover`, `hred`, `hn` and `hn0` require that the images of $i_1$ and $i_2$ cover the special fibre, that the scheme-theoretic intersection `pullback i₁.1 i₂.1` is reduced, and that its number of points equals $n$, with $0 < n$.
--
--   *Sections and relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ data.* Let $\varepsilon$ be a section of the two-chart model over $A$, and $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ sections of $c_1, c_2$, with `hε₁` asserting that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ is the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$. Let $D$ be a `RelativePic0Designation` for the two-chart model over $A$ (a scheme $D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ together with a zero section), with `hrep` asserting that $D$ represents the relative sub-Picard functor cut out by `algEquivZeroCut` (the condition `FibrewiseAlgEquivZero` on rigidified line bundles), and with $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ smooth and separated. The hypotheses `hreps` and `hPk` give the corresponding representability over $k$ for `D.baseChange k` together with an isomorphism between its Poincaré bundle and the base change of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some`; $D_1, D_2$ with `hrep₁`, `hrep₂` are representing designations for $c_1$ and $c_2$ over $k$. The morphism $\nu_2$ over the special-fibre Picard scheme to $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ is pinned by `hν₂`, which requires, for every $k$-scheme $t$ and every point $a$ of `(D.baseChange k).toBase` over $t$, an isomorphism between the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ and the `rigidify`-normalisation along $\varepsilon_2$ of the pullback, under the curve change attached to $i_2$, of the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` pulled back along $a$.
--
--   *Geometric fibre and its dictionary.* Fix embeddings of $A$ and $L$ into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, compatibly. Let $M\eta$ be a `CurveModel` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) and $e\eta$ an isomorphism of $M\eta.C$ with the base change of the two-chart model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, compatible with the structure morphisms (`heη`). The hypothesis `hMηpin` states that, under $M\eta$'s identification of its function field, every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) has Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the expansion of $a$ in $L(\!(q)\!)$; `hgal` states that for every automorphism $g$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M\eta.C$, if $x'$ composed into the two-chart model equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by the same composite for $x$, then $M\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x' = \mathrm{arithmeticGalois}(g) \cdot M\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x$, the action being the coefficientwise semilinear action of $g$ on places of the function field.
--
--   *Special-fibre group dictionary.* Let $G$ be a [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9), consisting of abelian groups $J_s^0$, $J_I$, $J_E$, a subgroup `torus` of $J_s^0$ and a surjective homomorphism $\mathrm{proj} : J_s^0 \to J_I \times J_E$ with kernel `torus`. Bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` identify $J_s^0$, $J_I$, $J_E$ with the $k$-points of `(D.baseChange k).toBase`, $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$; `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` require these bijections to be additive in the sense that the Poincaré pullback at a sum is isomorphic to the tensor product of the Poincaré pullbacks; `hproj` requires, for each $x \in J_s^0$, that `ptsI (G.proj x).1` is `pts x` followed by the morphism `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom` attached to $i_1$ and $\varepsilon_1$, and that `ptsE (G.proj x).2` is `pts x` followed by $\nu_2$.
--
--   *Generic group dictionary and Hecke action.* A bijection `gpts` identifies [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186) with the points of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, additively for the relative group law of `hrep.some` (`hgadd`). A map $\varphi$ from [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16) $= \mathbb{Z}[X_{\mathbb{P} \sqcup \mathbb{N}}]$ to endomorphisms of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ satisfies `hφmul` (each $\varphi(t)$ is additive for the relative group law on points over any base) and `hφpts` (for the module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129), `gpts (t • x)` is `gpts x` followed by $\varphi(t)$).
--
--   *Abel–Jacobi data.* The group `hDL`, `ajL`, `kL`, `ajbar`, `εbar`, `hPL`, `hajLε`, `hajL`, `hkL₁`, `hkL₂`, `hajbar`, `hajbar_over`, `hεbar`, `hεbar_aj`, `hpts_aj` (summarised here) provides: representability over $L$ for `D.baseChange L` with a base-change isomorphism of Poincaré bundles; an Abel–Jacobi morphism `ajL` over $L$ sending the base-changed section to the zero section and characterised by the condition that the Poincaré pullback along a point $x$ followed by `ajL` is the line bundle of the effective relative Cartier divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the section; the comparison morphism `kL` between the geometric pullbacks over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and over $L$, compatible with both projections; the induced map `ajbar` on $M\eta.C$, lying over the structure morphisms, and a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point `εbar` over the cusp section with `ajbar` annihilating it; and the statement that for $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x$ and $s$ of $M\eta.C$ with $s$ lying over $\varepsilon$ there is a degree-zero divisor equal to $[\,\mathrm{place}(x)\,] - [\,\mathrm{place}(s)\,]$ whose class under `gpts` is $x$ followed by `ajbar`.
--
--   *Igusa cusp component.* Let $w$ be an `IntegralWeightOneForm` for $k$ and $M$, let $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ be a curve model over $k$ of the Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), and $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`he₁`), with the relevant chart preimage non-empty. The Gauss-reading hypothesis `hgauss₁` requires: for every $a$ in the finite chart algebra and all power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having non-zero reduction in $k$ and $a \cdot y = x$ in $L(\!(q)\!)$, the element of the Igusa function field obtained from $a$ through $e_1$, $i_1$ and the finite chart has Laurent expansion the quotient of the reductions of $x$ and of $y$.
--
--   An additive isomorphism $\theta_1 : J_I \cong \mathrm{Pic}^0(k, \mathrm{Ig})$ is pinned by `hθpin₁`: for $g \in J_I$ and a $k$-point $x$ of $c_1$, if the Poincaré pullback at `ptsI g` is isomorphic to the line bundle of the divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of $\varepsilon_1$, then $\theta_1 g$ is the class of $[\,\mathrm{place}(x)\,] - [\,\mathrm{place}(\varepsilon_1)\,]$, places being computed through $e_1^{-1}$ in $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$. Finally `frobIg` is an element of `SemilinearAut k (igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w)` acting on Laurent coefficients by $c \mapsto c^p$ in every degree (`hfrobIg`).
--
--   *Norm-free abelian subscheme.* Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a scheme over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ with a closed immersion $\iota$ over $A$ into $D.\mathrm{toBase}$, with $\mathcal{A} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ proper and smooth, with connected geometric fibres over every algebraically closed field (`h𝒜conn`), closed under unit, multiplication and inversion for the relative group law (`h𝒜grp`), stable under every $\varphi(t)$ (`h𝒜hecke`), and with `h𝒜gen`: for $x \in J_1(Mp)$, $x$ lies in [`ModularCurve.normFreePartAt (M * p) p`](def/ModularCurve_X1PrimitiveSpecializationAtP.html#L29) (the image of `normFreeEnd (M * p) (normFreeRepsAt (M * p) p)`) if and only if `gpts x` factors through $\iota$.
--
--   *Place data.* Let $Pl$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its non-units, $\rho : A \to Pl$ compatible with the structural map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $O$ a subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ contained in $Pl$ with $\rho_O : A \to O$ likewise compatible, and $\pi_k : Pl \to k$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,k = \pi_k \circ \rho$; $\pi_k$ is assumed surjective.
--
--   *Conclusion.* For every $x \in J_1(Mp) =$ [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), all points $z, z'$ of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho_O$, and all $y, y' \in J_s^0$: if $x$ lies in [`ModularCurve.normFreePartAt (M * p) p`](def/ModularCurve_X1PrimitiveSpecializationAtP.html#L29); if `gpts x` equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $O \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $z$; if `pts y` followed by the projection of `D.baseChange k` to $D.P$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\pi_k$ composed with the inclusion $O \hookrightarrow Pl$, followed by $z$; if $z'$ is $z$ followed by $\varphi$ of the Hecke generator [`ModularCurve.heckeGenOne ⟨p, Fact.out⟩`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L18) (the indeterminate indexed by the prime $p$); if `pts y'` followed by the same projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of that residue map followed by $z'$; and if $(G.\mathrm{proj}\,y).2 = 0$ in $J_E$; then
--   $$\theta_1\bigl((G.\mathrm{proj}\,y').1\bigr) = (p : \mathbb{Z}) \cdot \bigl(\mathrm{frobIg}^{-1} \cdot \theta_1((G.\mathrm{proj}\,y).1)\bigr)$$
--   in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the Igusa function field over $k$, the inner action being that of the inverse of the coefficientwise Frobenius through `SemilinearAut`.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura congruence at $p$ read on the cusp (Igusa) component of the Néron special fibre of $J_1(Mp)$: the Hecke operator at $p$ acts on the $J_I$-coordinate as multiplication by $p$ composed with the inverse of the coefficientwise Frobenius, with no diamond twist, for those special-fibre points that arise as reductions of $O$-points of the norm-free part. It is used by the statements about the norm-free family which compute the Hecke action and the pairing on the Igusa component in the level-lowering argument at $p$.
